the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 30.

the fluents are:
    *a vehicle* is at *a place* heading *a direction*; known as location; synonym the heading of *a vehicle* at *a place* is *a direction*.
    there is a collision warning between *a first vehicle* and *a second vehicle* at *a place*; known as collisionWarning.
    *a first vehicle* has the right of way over *a second vehicle* at *a place*; known as rightOfWay.
    there is a possible collision between *a first vehicle* and *a second vehicle*; known as collisionPossible.

the events are:
    *a vehicle* is sent to *a destination*; known as destination.
    *a vehicle* is removed; known as remove.
    *a vehicle* drives along *a route* towards *a destination*; known as drive.

the actions are:
    *a vehicle* steps from *a place* to *a next place*; known as step.
    *a vehicle* turns *a direction*; known as turn.

the templates are:
    *a place* is at column *a number* and row *a second number*.
    appending *a first route* to *a second route* gives *a third route*.
    the directions from *a start* to *a finish* are *a route*.
    the orientation from *a first place* to *a second place* is *a direction*.
    there is a route from *a start* to *a finish* along *a long route*.
    *a place* is on *a street*.
    *a first place* is next to *a second place* going *a direction*.
    *a first direction* is opposite to *a second direction*.
    *a first direction* clashes with *a second direction*.
    *a direction* runs horizontally.
    *a direction* runs vertically.
    *a first direction* is to the right of *a second direction*.
    there are crossroads at *a place*.
    *a street* has priority at the junction at *a place*.

the knowledge base self driving cars includes:

% A place is written column-row, as in 2-1.
% A route is written as its first leg followed by the rest of the route, and each leg is a
% direction and a street. So [[northward, westStreet], [[eastward, northStreet], []]] means:
% north along westStreet, then east along northStreet, then nothing more ([] is the empty route).
% Written this way, the three rules for driving can tell a route of one leg from a longer one
% by its shape alone, as the original program does.
initially mycar is at 2-1 heading northward
    and yourcar is at 6-1 heading northward
    and othercar is at 10-5 heading westward
    and troubleMaker is at 6-2 heading northward
    and brokencar is at 2-7 heading noward.

% Just for fun.
when a vehicle is removed
then it is not the case that the vehicle is at a place heading a direction.

% The main rule, which controls the behaviour of the system.
if a vehicle is sent to a destination to a first time
    and the vehicle is at a place heading a direction at the first time
then the directions from the place to the destination are a route
    and the vehicle drives along the route towards the destination from the first time.

% Finding directions is easiest when the start and finish are on the same street.
the directions from a start to a finish are a route if
    the start is on a street
    and the finish is on the street
    and the orientation from the start to the finish is a direction
    and the route = [[the direction, the street], []].

the orientation from a first place to a second place is northward if
    the first place is at column a number and row a second number
    and the second place is at column the number and row a third number
    and the second number < the third number.

the orientation from a first place to a second place is southward if
    the first place is at column a number and row a second number
    and the second place is at column the number and row a third number
    and the second number > the third number.

the orientation from a first place to a second place is eastward if
    the first place is at column a number and row a second number
    and the second place is at column a third number and row the second number
    and the number < the third number.

the orientation from a first place to a second place is westward if
    the first place is at column a number and row a second number
    and the second place is at column a third number and row the second number
    and the number > the third number.

% Otherwise, directions can be found in a database of long distance routes,
% by taking the part of a route that joins the start's street to the finish's street.
the directions from a start to a finish are a route if
    the finish is on a second street
    and there is a route from a first place to a second place along a long route
    and appending a first part to [[a second direction, the second street], a remainder] gives the long route
    and the start is on a first street
    and appending a beginning to [[a first direction, the first street], a link] gives the first part
    and appending [[the first direction, the first street], the link] to [[the second direction, the second street], []] gives the route.

% Some long distance routes.
there is a route from 2-9 to 9-9 along [[eastward, northStreet], []].
there is a route from 2-1 to 9-9 along [[northward, westStreet], [[eastward, northStreet], []]].
there is a route from 6-1 to 9-9 along [[northward, highStreet], [[eastward, northStreet], []]].
there is a route from 9-9 to 2-1 along [[westward, northStreet], [[southward, westStreet], []]].
there is a route from 10-5 to 6-1 along [[westward, mainStreet], [[southward, highStreet], []]].

% Some street locations.
a place is on mainStreet if
    the place is at column a number and row 5
    and 3 =< the number
    and the number =< 10.

a place is on northStreet if
    the place is at column a number and row 9
    and 2 =< the number
    and the number =< 9.

a place is on highStreet if
    the place is at column 6 and row a number
    and 1 =< the number
    and the number =< 9.

a place is on westStreet if
    the place is at column 2 and row a number
    and 1 =< the number
    and the number =< 9.

a place is on eastStreet if
    the place is at column 8 and row a number
    and 1 =< the number
    and the number =< 9.

% There are three cases for driving. In all three, driving starts at the first time,
% but stepping forward starts at the third time: the vehicle may have to wait for the step to be possible.
a vehicle drives along [[a direction, a street], []] towards a destination from a first time to a second time if
    the vehicle is at a place heading the direction at the first time
    and the place is different from the destination
    and the place is next to a next place going the direction
    and the next place is on the street
    and the vehicle steps from the place to the next place from a third time to a fourth time
    and the vehicle drives along [[the direction, the street], []] towards the destination from the fourth time to the second time.

a vehicle drives along [[a first direction, a first street], [[a second direction, a second street], a tail]] towards a destination from a first time to a second time if
    the vehicle is at a place heading the first direction at a third time
    and the place is next to a next place going the first direction
    and it is not the case that the next place is on the second street
    and the vehicle steps from the place to the next place from a fourth time to a fifth time
    and the vehicle drives along [[the first direction, the first street], [[the second direction, the second street], the tail]] towards the destination from the fifth time to the second time.

% Here stepping and turning happen together.
a vehicle drives along [[a first direction, a first street], [[a second direction, a second street], a tail]] towards a destination from a first time to a second time if
    the vehicle is at a place heading the first direction at a third time
    and the place is next to a next place going the first direction
    and the next place is on the second street
    and the vehicle steps from the place to the next place from a fourth time to a fifth time
    and the vehicle turns the second direction from the fourth time to the fifth time
    and the vehicle drives along [[the second direction, the second street], the tail] towards the destination from the fifth time to the second time.

% Stepping and turning update the current state.
when a vehicle steps from a place to a next place
then the vehicle is at the place heading a direction that is the place becomes the next place.

when a vehicle turns a direction
then the heading of the vehicle at a place that is a second direction becomes the direction.

% Some geography.
a first place is next to a second place going northward if
    the first place is at column a number and row a second number
    and a third number = the second number + 1
    and the second place is at column the number and row the third number.

a first place is next to a second place going southward if
    the first place is at column a number and row a second number
    and a third number = the second number - 1
    and the second place is at column the number and row the third number.

a first place is next to a second place going eastward if
    the first place is at column a number and row a second number
    and a third number = the number + 1
    and the second place is at column the third number and row the second number.

a first place is next to a second place going westward if
    the first place is at column a number and row a second number
    and a third number = the number - 1
    and the second place is at column the third number and row the second number.

% Some self-preservation.
it must not be true that
    a vehicle steps from a place to a next place
    and there is a possible collision between the vehicle and a second vehicle.

there is a possible collision between a first vehicle and a second vehicle at a time if
    the first vehicle is at a first place heading a first direction at the time
    and the first place is next to a second place going the first direction
    and the second vehicle is at the second place heading a second direction at the time
    and it is not the case that the first direction is opposite to the second direction.

northward is opposite to southward.
southward is opposite to northward.
eastward is opposite to westward.
westward is opposite to eastward.

% Some rules of the road, which are conducive to a well-ordered society.
it must not be true that
    a vehicle steps from a place to a next place
    and there is a collision warning between the vehicle and a second vehicle at the next place
    and it is not the case that the vehicle has the right of way over the second vehicle at the next place.

there is a collision warning between a first vehicle and a second vehicle at a next place at a time if
    the first vehicle is at a first place heading a first direction at the time
    and the second vehicle is at a second place heading a second direction at the time
    and the first place is next to the next place going the first direction
    and the second place is next to the next place going the second direction
    and the first direction clashes with the second direction.

a first direction clashes with a second direction if
    the first direction runs horizontally
    and the second direction runs vertically.

a first direction clashes with a second direction if
    the first direction runs vertically
    and the second direction runs horizontally.

eastward runs horizontally.
westward runs horizontally.
northward runs vertically.
southward runs vertically.

a first vehicle has the right of way over a second vehicle at a next place at a time if
    a street has priority at the junction at the next place
    and the first vehicle is at a place heading a direction at the time
    and the place is on the street.

a first vehicle has the right of way over a second vehicle at a next place at a time if
    there are crossroads at the next place
    and the first vehicle is at a first place heading a first direction at a second time
    and the second vehicle is at a second place heading a second direction at the second time
    and the first direction is to the right of the second direction.

westward is to the right of northward.
southward is to the right of westward.
eastward is to the right of southward.
northward is to the right of eastward.

% Cross roads and T junctions can be derived from street locations,
% but for this simple example it is easier just to list them.
there are crossroads at 6-5.
there are crossroads at 8-5.

westStreet has priority at the junction at 2-5.
northStreet has priority at the junction at 6-9.
northStreet has priority at the junction at 8-9.

% The one bridge to Prolog: Logical English has no way of its own to take the pair 2-1 apart.
a place is at column a number X and row a second number Y if
    prolog (the place = X-Y).

% Joining two routes, one after the other.
appending [] to a route gives the route.

appending [a leg, a first route] to a second route gives [the leg, a third route] if
    appending the first route to the second route gives the third route.

scenario one is:
    mycar is sent to 2-9 from 2 to 3.
    troubleMaker is sent to 8-9 from 2 to 3.
    yourcar is sent to 9-9 from 2 to 3.
    othercar is sent to 6-1 from 1 to 2.
    brokencar is removed from 15 to 16.
